# GitHub Local Index (repo workspace)

When working in this repository:

1. **Read first:** `.github-local-indexer/INDEX.md` or `status.json`
2. **Check cache age:** `last_indexed_at`, `index_age_minutes`, `refresh_recommended`
3. **Search locally:** `.cursor/bin/github-local-indexer search "<query>" --json`
4. **Refresh cache when stale** (see commands below); mention age to the user
5. **Do not** call GitHub API unless index is empty or user explicitly asks for remote

## Refresh cache (agent)

```bash
# Check if refresh needed
.cursor/bin/github-local-indexer status --json

# Pull latest from GitHub into local index (GITHUB_TOKEN required)
.cursor/bin/github-local-indexer sync owner/repo --wait

# Add repo then sync (first time)
.cursor/bin/github-local-indexer repo add owner/repo
.cursor/bin/github-local-indexer sync owner/repo --wait
```

Refresh when `refresh_recommended: true`, `freshness: stale`, or `index_age_minutes` > `stale_ttl_minutes` (15).
